                <pb facs="0451" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.50/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-11T11:00:00-04:00">September 11, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>238. Referring to my telegram No. 225 of August 28, 11 a.m. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">3 p.m.</hi>] and previous correspondence concerning
                    economic collaboration in development of national resources of Bolivia, Minister
                    of Foreign Affairs has again asked very earnestly that the United States
                    Government make some public statement regarding progress of arrangements to send
                    down technical commission and this commission come with as little delay as
                    possible. The Minister says that criticism of delay is growing in and out of
                    Bolivian Congress and he is most anxious to announce here as early as possible
                    when technical experts may be expected to arrive. I hope that the Department
                    will be able to telegraph me some message to give to Dr. Ostria Gutiérrez.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
